{"id": "section-body-14594", "title": "Corneal Ulcer", "chapterId": "chapter-fourteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "EYE DISEASES AND REFRACTIVE ERRORS", "Painful Red Eyes", "Corneal Ulcer"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-14594", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Corneal Ulcer", "runs": [{"text": "Corneal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Ulcer"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1271"}}, {"id": "body-14595", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "This is a painful red eye condition resulting from a raw discontinuity to the corneal epithelium. It may be caused by infection (bacterial, viral e.g., Herpes simplex virus and measles, fungal, trauma (physical or chemical) and nutritional (Vitamin A deficiency). Systemic conditions can contribute to corneal ulcers as well.", "runs": [{"text": "This is a painful red eye condition resulting from a raw discontinuity to the corneal epithelium. It may be caused by infection (bacterial, viral e.g., Herpes simplex virus and measles, fungal, trauma (physical or chemical) and nutritional (Vitamin A deficiency). Systemic conditions can contribute to corneal ulcers as well."}]}, {"id": "body-14598", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-14599", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Painful and red eye of acute onset", "runs": [{"text": "Painful"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "red"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "eye"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acute"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "onset"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1265"}}, {"id": "body-14600", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Excessive tearing", "runs": [{"text": "Excessive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tearing"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1265"}}, {"id": "bod